@filipesilva wrote
> I think we need to change the code in`@angular/core` to not have errors when `ngDevMode` is not defined.

But we have such code here: https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/939529ce5dcc7a526a67d45723fbd8ede83d7750/packages/core/src/util/ng_dev_mode.ts#L110-L112 So there is something else going on. Did that code got somehow removed?

I followed the steps in https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/31595#issuecomment-519129090 and was able to see the error again as @mcalmus reported. I had to set `"enableIvy": false` in `tsconfig.json` and use `ng serve --prod --source-map` to get good source maps.

The error came from this line:
https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/04ddcfecd8134e4c57ce95ce35444d1e26b424a3/packages/core/src/core.ts#L42-L52

This is indeed a problem because this line is a toplevel side effect that checks a variable that might not exist at the toplevel. It needs to treated similarly as other toplevel side effects were in https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/32079, preferably in such a way that doesn't have a leftover side effect like it does now in the [side-effects test](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/04ddcfecd8134e4c57ce95ce35444d1e26b424a3/integration/side-effects/snapshots/core/esm2015.js#L5-L17) (cc @petebacondarwin).

If I replace it `if (false) {` the error goes away so I think it should be ok.

Your report of the 1404 line is worrisome though... It's this done:
```
function initNgDevMode() {
    // The below checks are to ensure that calling `initNgDevMode` multiple times does not
    // reset the counters.
    // If the `ngDevMode` is not an object, then it means we have not created the perf counters
    // yet.
    if (typeof ngDevMode === 'undefined' || ngDevMode) {
        if (typeof ngDevMode !== 'object') {
            ngDevModeResetPerfCounters(); 
        }
        return !!ngDevMode; //    <----- this is 1404
    }
    return false;
}
```

I'm not sure how you get there but it makes sense that it's a problem, because `ngDevMode` is initialized in `ngDevModeResetPerfCounters` only. I think this logic needs to be revisited.
